Database migrations for MentorMatch.

The legacy_baseline revision represents the existing schema before admin flags.
The admin_flags_v1 revision adds is_admin and is_active.

From the backend directory, upgrade a new empty database with:

    python -m app.init_db

For an existing unversioned PostgreSQL database, use the guarded helper from
the backend directory. It compares the reflected schema, makes and checks a
fresh backup, asks you to confirm the exact target, adds only recognized
missing schema objects, then stamps and upgrades:

    read -rsp 'Target PostgreSQL URL: ' MENTORMATCH_TARGET_DATABASE_URL
    printf '\n'
    export MENTORMATCH_TARGET_DATABASE_URL
    python scripts/db_safety.py preflight
    python scripts/db_safety.py adopt --directory "$HOME/mentor_match_backups"

Create the backup directory outside the project. The helper does not read
.env, print credentials, or seed records. It stops on differences outside the
specifically recognized add-only changes. A dump archive listing and checksum
are verified; restore it to a separate database to rehearse recovery before
production use.
